0. The CHARMM C27 FF we have been using was inherited from Brooks lab 2004-2007.
   The CMAP it includes is different from the distributed C27 FF.
   This directory inlcudes the distributed version (C22+CMAP from toppar_c36_aug14.tgz)
   and CpHMD top & par.

1. top_all22_prot.rtf
   Distributed C22 protein topology file

2. par_all22_prot.prm
   Distributed C22 protein parameter file + CMAP

3. toppar_water_ions.str
   Distributed C22 top & par for water and ions

4. radius_gbsw.str
   Distributed C22 atomic input radii for GBSW

5. toppar_phmd_c22.str
   CpHMD top & par.
   Copied from toppar_phmd_c36.str; change ASPP2/ASPP1/GLUP2/GLUP1 top & par back to C22

6. phmd_hybrid_g2_c22.in
   Model compound PMF parameters for hybrid solvent CpHMD
   Copied from phmd_hybrid_g2_shane.in, revise format

7. Usage of distributed C27 FF with CpHMD toppar.
   The strategy is not to touch distributed C27 FF but make our CpHMD toppar as a
   stream file (toppar_phmd_c22.str). After regular toppar has been read in, stream
   CpHMD toppar. Commands are:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
! Set variables
! -------------
set top     = XXX/top_all22_prot.rtf           ! C27 protein topology file
set par     = XXX/par_all22_prot.prm           ! C27 protein parameter file
set wation  = XXX/toppar_water_ions.str        ! C27 top & par for water & ions
set phmdtp  = XXX/toppar_phmd_c22.str          ! C27 CpHMD top & par files

! Read topology and parameter files
! ---------------------------------
open unit 1 read form name @top
read rtf card unit 1
close unit 1

open unit 1 read form name @par
read param card unit 1 flex ! must use flex here
close unit 1

stream @wation

stream @phmdtp
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
